  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation of Gender-Based Violence Prevention Plans and Autonomy Promotion of Former FARC Women Combatants in Transit to Civil Life in Colombia (Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the previous project on Strategy for Trainers and Promoters for the Prevention of Gender-Based Violence (GBV), developed in 2017-2018, this project focuses on the creation, strengthening and implementation of prevention plans led by groups, committees or &#x201c;gender tables&#x201d; in the prioritized regions, where promoters for the prevention of GBV graduated from the course carried out in the previous phase. The objective is to contribute to the individual and collective political, social and economic autonomy of former Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia (FARC) women combatants as they transition to civilian life.</narrative>
  </description>
